Haskell 1.2 libraries for Yale Haskell.

prelude/   the standard prelude used by the system (with Yale changes:
           optimizer annotations, monadic I/O primitives, Lisp primitives)
hbc/       libraries ported from the Chalmers hbc distribution
cl/        libraries implemented through the Haskell <-> Lisp interface
X11/       the CLX-based X window interface (not currently built)

These are kept unchanged while the Haskell 98 libraries are developed
alongside them (see doc/REVIVAL-PLAN.md).
